# P2P Architecture Rules

- Roles: **Host** (source of truth) & **Client**; same code, role decided at runtime.
- WebRTC via `peerjs`; default channel streams Redux actions & snapshots.
- Message types defined in `src/services/p2p/events.ts`; update both host & client handlers when adding.
- Maintain deterministic state: clients forward actions, host broadcasts snapshots.
- Reconnect: clients retry every 2 s (max 5); send `request-sync` on reconnect.
- Security: validate incoming actions against schema; (future) token handshake.
- Keep protocol backward-compatible: add `protocolVersion` when breaking changes.
- Limit in-memory snapshots to last **5** for quick replay.
